                    "rel": "external_reference",
                    "text": "Planning the Implementation and Deployment of Secure Development Practices"
                  },
                  {
                    "href": "#79b86445-1dc2-497e-9097-6ae5bcc36c4b",
                    "rel": "external_reference",
                    "text": "3.1.2, 3.2.1, 3.2.2, 3.3.1, 3.4.2, 3.4.3"
                  },
                  {
                    "href": "#4c47252a-3356-45a7-b474-556c33d13ae4",
                    "rel": "external_reference",
                    "text": "SA-1, SA-8, SA-15, SR-3"
                  },
                  {
                    "href": "#0aa5e31f-31d7-41bd-8ae9-dd68229f683c",
                    "rel": "external_reference",
                    "text": "T0414; K0003, K0039, K0044, K0157, K0168, K0177, K0211, K0260, K0261, K0262, K0524; S0010, S0357, S0368; A0033, A0123, A0151"
                  },
                  {
                    "href": "#4f517150-7171-44ba-ae0c-5fb1f2b3a3f8",
                    "rel": "external_reference",
                    "text": "SA-1, SA-8, SA-15, SR-3"
                  }
                ],
                "parts": [
                  {
                    "id": "statement_PO.1.1",
                    "name": "statement",
                    "prose": "Identify and document all security requirements for the organization’s software development infrastructures and processes, and maintain the requirements over time."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "PO.1.1.1",
                    "name": "example",
                    "title": "Example 1:",
                    "prose": "Define policies for securing software development infrastructures and their components, including development endpoints, throughout the SDLC and maintaining that security."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "PO.1.1.2",
                    "name": "example",
                    "title": "Example 2:",
                    "prose": "Define policies for securing software development processes throughout the SDLC and maintaining that security, including for open-source and other third-party software components utilized by software being developed."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "PO.1.1.3",
                    "name": "example",
                    "title": "Example 3:",
                    "prose": "Review and update security requirements at least annually, or sooner if there are new requirements from internal or external sources, or a major security incident targeting software development infrastructure has occurred."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "PO.1.1.4",
                    "name": "example",
                    "title": "Example 4:",
                    "prose": "Educate affected individuals on impending changes to requirements."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
